        ]
      },
      "abstract": "<jats:p>We prove new bounds for how often Dirichlet polynomials can take large values. This gives improved estimates for a Dirichlet polynomial of length $N$ taking values of size close to $N^{3/4}$, which is the critical situation for several estimates in analytic number theory connected to prime numbers and the Riemann zeta function. As a consequence, we deduce a zero density estimate $N(\\sigma,T)\\le T^{30(1-\\sigma)/13+o(1)}$ and asymptotics for primes in short intervals of length $x^{17/30+o(1)}$.</jats:p>",
